Subject: Overwrite Object Literal Slots Inline Instead Of Defining Them

What this does
  `OP_define_field` -- what every non-computed `key: value` in an object
  literal compiles to -- overwrites an existing plain data property directly
  instead of calling JS_DefinePropertyValue once per field.

Why we need it
  A literal built from a shape template arrives with every slot already present
  as JS_UNDEFINED with flags exactly JS_PROP_C_W_E, so every store was a
  re-define: find_own_property, the LENGTH test, check_define_prop_flags, the
  AUTOINIT test, the getset/varref branch cluster and two
  js_update_property_flags calls that are provably no-ops, all behind a
  six-argument non-inlined call. `o.a = v` has an inline cache; the literal path
  had nothing.

What it adds
  One lookup and one flag test. The overwrite happens only when the receiver is
  an ordinary object and the atom is already an own property with exactly
  JS_PROP_C_W_E and no TMASK bits. GETSET, VARREF and AUTOINIT keep the generic
  path, JS_PROP_LENGTH is excluded so an Array's length is never touched here,
  and the autoinit, flag-update and inline-cache watchpoint work the generic
  call would do is a no-op by construction. A literal site wider than
  JS_OBJLIT_MAX_PROPS is not templated, so its defines are inserts and the
  lookup is not amortised: that shape measures 2-4% slower and is stated in the
  notes.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -22079,9 +22079,26 @@
             {
                 int ret;
                 JSAtom atom;
+                JSObject *p;
+                JSProperty *pr;
+                JSShapeProperty *prs;
                 atom = get_u32(pc);
                 pc += 4;
 
+                if (likely(JS_VALUE_GET_TAG(sp[-2]) == JS_TAG_OBJECT)) {
+                    p = JS_VALUE_GET_OBJ(sp[-2]);
+                    if (likely(!p->is_exotic)) {
+                        prs = find_own_property(&pr, p, atom);
+                        if (likely(prs != NULL &&
+                                   (prs->flags & (JS_PROP_TMASK | JS_PROP_C_W_E |
+                                                  JS_PROP_LENGTH)) == JS_PROP_C_W_E)) {
+                            set_value(ctx, &pr->u.value, sp[-1]);
+                            sp--;
+                            BREAK;
+                        }
+                    }
+                }
+
                 ret = JS_DefinePropertyValue(ctx, sp[-2], atom, sp[-1],
                                              JS_PROP_C_W_E | JS_PROP_THROW);
                 sp--;
